    "result_text": "The full suite is green (32 tests, 0 failures/errors, BUILD SUCCESS).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the audit-on-create requirement for the create-owner endpoint.\n\n**What changed:**\n\n1. **New function class** \u2014 `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/AuditOwnerCreated.java`. A single-step function that reads the persisted owner (`@Val Owner`) and emits one line on the SLF4J logger named `AUDIT`, containing the owner id, `customerCode`, and `registrationDate` (rendered as ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` via `LocalDate.toString()`, matching the response serialization).\n\n2. **Pipeline wiring** \u2014 `src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`. Inserted an `audit` step between `save` and `respond`. Placement after `save` is deliberate: the owner id is only assigned once persisted, so the audit step runs on the fully-populated entity. It carries `govern: [ transaction ]` consistent with the surrounding steps.\n\nThe emission is genuinely tied to a successful create \u2014 it sits after all validation/uniqueness/capacity guards and after the save, so a rejected request never produces an audit line.\n\n**Verification:** the new `Cp21Tests.coreLogsAuditOnCreate` passes (the emitted line was `AUDIT - Owner created: id=11 customerCode=TOW-SUR-0001 registrationDate=2026-08-14`), and the full suite runs 32 tests with 0 failures/errors.",
